      "retrieved": "2026-10-14",
      "revision": 1379873128,
      "text": "Prunus rivularis, known variously by the common names creek plum, hog plum, or wild-goose plum is a thicket-forming shrub in the rose family, Rosaceae. It is a deciduous shrub consisting of slender stems with umbel clusters of white blossoms. The fruit is a drupe that resembles a large berry."
